{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SeparatedRepresentation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SeparatedRepresentation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SeparatedHeight","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.Basic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_indep_le_degreeOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_indep_le_degreeOf","kind":"theorem","line":484,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L484-L499","doc":"**Mahler's `n ≤ r_m + 1`.**  For a single split-off variable of degree at most `d`, a\nminimum separated representation has at most `d + 1` terms.\n\nThis is the bound the recursion's row cost needs: with `t = r/D₁` and `r ≤ d + 1`, the growth\ncondition (`RothGrowth`, which makes the split-off variable's degree the *smallest*) turns `t`\ninto something of order `1/ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_indep_card_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_indep_card_le","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L465-L482","doc":"**A minimum representation, with its length bounded by the number of `y`-monomials.**\n\nThe bound is what makes the induction step's error term `t = r/D₁` affordable: grouping on the\n`x`-side gives `r = #{x\\text{-monomials}}`, which is a *product* of degrees; grouping on the\n`y`-side gives one term per `y`-monomial, and the shortening can only reduce that. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_indep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_indep","kind":"theorem","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L456-L462","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_indep_representation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_indep_representation","kind":"theorem","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L429-L454","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_shorter_of_phi_dep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_shorter_of_phi_dep","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L372-L427","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_shorter_of_psi_dep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_shorter_of_psi_dep","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L313-L369","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.degreeOf_factor_le_of_indep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.degreeOf_factor_le_of_indep","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L266-L300","doc":"**The factors of a separated representation have degrees bounded by the polynomial's**,\nprovided the *other* family is linearly independent.\n\nThe proof is the disjointness identity again: a non-zero coefficient of `φ k` gives a non-zero\nvector `c`, independence of `ψ` makes `∑ cₗψₗ` non-zero, and any non-zero coefficient of that\nis a coefficient of `P` at a multi-index whose `σ`-part is the one we started with. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_image_snd_le_of_degreeOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_image_snd_le_of_degreeOf","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L228-L251","doc":"**Mahler's `n ≤ r_m + 1`**, for a single split-off variable.\n\nWith `τ = Unit` a `y`-part is determined by one exponent, and that exponent is at most the\ndegree of `P` in the split-off variable.  So the number of distinct `y`-parts — and hence, by\nthe results above, the representation length — is at most `d + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_fin_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_fin_right","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L197-L226","doc":"The `Fin r`-indexed form, with `r` pinned to the number of distinct `y`-parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_monomial_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_monomial_right","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L153-L195","doc":"**The mirror of `exists_separated_representation_monomial`: group by the `y`-part.**\n\nNow the *right* factors are bare monomials and the left ones collect the coefficients, so the\ncount is the number of distinct `y`-parts.\n\n**The grouped coefficients inherit `P`'s `x`-degrees.**  `φ j` is a sum of monomials whose\nexponents are the `x`-parts of `P`'s own support, so every exponent occurring in `φ j` occurs\nin `P`.\n\n⚠⚠ **That clause was missing, and without it `hres` cannot be discharged at all.**\n`RothLemmaUniform` at `m − 1` asks for `degreeOf j (φ k) ≤ d₁ j`; nothing anywhere in the chain\nfrom `P` down to `φ` recorded *any* bound on the factors' degrees, so the induction hypothesis\nhad no way to apply to the separated representation the induction step constructs.  §7 supplies\nit on the source's side — \"the degrees of `U` in `x₁,…,x_{m−1}` do not exceed `ρ₁,…,ρ_{m−1}`\" —\nand the arc had the length bound `n ≤ r_m + 1` from the same construction but not this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.degreeOf_monomial_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.degreeOf_monomial_le","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L144-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_fin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_fin","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L111-L130","doc":"**The `Fin r`-indexed form**, which is what `det_separated_wronskian` and the\nbounded-order Wronskian criterion actually consume, together with independence of the `φ`.\n\nReindexing is `Finset.equivFin`; independence transports because `equivFin.symm` is injective.\n\n⚠ Still only the `φ` are independent.  See the module header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L104-L109","doc":"Distinct monomials are linearly independent: they are part of `basisMonomials`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L75-L102","doc":"**A separated representation with linearly independent `φ`.**\n\nGrouping the monomials of `P` by their `x`-part makes the left factors *distinct* monomials,\nwhich `linearIndependent_monomial` shows are independent.  The `ψ` collect the corresponding\n`y`-parts.\n\n⚠ The `ψ` need not be independent, and Roth's lemma wants a representation where both families\nare — see the module header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_separated_representation","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L58-L73","doc":"**Every polynomial has a separated representation**, indexed by its own support.\n\nThe crude version: one term per monomial of `P`.  ⚠ Its `φ` are *not* independent — distinct\nmonomials of `P` can share an `x`-part.  Use the grouped version below when independence\nmatters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.monomial_sumElim_eq'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.monomial_sumElim_eq'","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L50-L56","doc":"The same split with the coefficient on the *right* factor — the orientation the grouped\nrepresentation below needs, since there the left factors are bare monomials. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.monomial_sumElim_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.monomial_sumElim_eq","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedRepresentation.lean#L43-L48","doc":"A monomial on `σ ⊕ τ` splits as a product, with the coefficient on the left factor. ","signatureChunk":0}]}